# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/skinning-leatherworking
title Skinning + Leatherworking 1-300
category Professions
kind profession
skills Skinning, Leatherworking
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Skinning and Leatherworking 1-300 together, for both factions: each Leatherworking stretch starts
# with a Skinning loop sized to what that stretch needs, which also raises Skinning, and the craft
# follows with the materials in your bags. Spares carry to the next stretch, and when a stretch
# needs what Skinning cannot gather yet, Skinning catches up first. Skinning ranks are trained at
# the Leatherworking trainer visit when the skill allows. Skinning reaches 300 before the last
# Leatherworking stretch.
#
# The Skinning loops are the Skinning guide's (densest ground at a safe level, picked where you
# are); the Leatherworking route, its recipes, trainers, vendor goods and counts the Leatherworking
# guide's (enough for 9 players in 10). Anything Skinning does not give is bought or farmed as there
# (Gather, Buy or Mix).
#
# ASSUMED: how far Skinning rises on a stretch's materials is the Skinning guide's expected
# skill-ups per node on the band's loops and what players' recorded gathers gave per node, averaged
# over the band's loops.
# About 19 hours of skinning in 12 gathering stretches; it gathers about 1240 Thick Leather, 970
# Rugged Leather, 290 Heavy Leather, 250 Light Leather, 160 Heavy Scorpid Scale and 150 Medium
# Leather.
#
# Leatherworking cures hides and stitches leather into armour and armour kits. Skinning is its
# partner: leather is most of what the route costs, and every leather on it is one you can skin
# yourself. Hides are a rare find when skinning, so the route gets them from the Auction House (the
# ones you skin count too); the salt, threads and dyes come from vendors.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Leatherworking trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes
# only up to 50); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers, who teach the recipes up to 150;
# Expert from level 20 (50s) at Telonis in Darnassus or Una in Thunder Bluff; Artisan from level 35
# at Drakk Stonehand in Aerie Peak or Hahrana Ironhide in Camp Mojache.
#
# Two patterns come from vendors: Wicked Leather Gauntlets (Leonard Porter in the Western
# Plaguelands, Werg Thickblade in Tirisfal Glades) and Runic Leather Headband (Jase Farlane at
# Light's Hope Chapel). Patterns that need a Tanning Rack or a Sewing Machine are left out: no town
# has either.
#
# The route (crafts are about what it takes; yellow and green recipes can take a few more):
# Apprentice (1-60), from level 1:
#    1-30  35 Light Leather: 105 Ruined Leather Scraps
#   30-40  10 Cured Light Hide: 10 Light Hide, 10 Salt
#   40-60  20 Embossed Leather Gloves: 60 Light Leather, 40 Coarse Thread
# Journeyman (60-150), from level 10:
#   60-70  10 Embossed Leather Gloves: 30 Light Leather, 20 Coarse Thread
#   70-80  10 Embossed Leather Pants: 60 Light Leather, 20 Coarse Thread, 10 Cured Light Hide
#   80-95  20 Cured Medium Hide: 20 Medium Hide, 20 Salt
#   95-105 22 Fine Leather Belt: 132 Light Leather, 44 Coarse Thread
#  105-125 20 Dark Leather Belt: 40 Fine Thread, 20 Cured Medium Hide, 20 Fine Leather Belt, 20 Gray Dye
#  125-130 8 Heavy Leather: 40 Medium Leather
#  130-143 25 Cured Heavy Hide: 25 Heavy Hide, 75 Salt
#  143-150 8 Hillman's Leather Gloves: 112 Medium Leather, 32 Fine Thread
# Expert (150-205), from level 20:
#  150-165 15 Barbaric Shoulders: 30 Fine Thread, 120 Heavy Leather, 15 Cured Heavy Hide
#  165-175 10 Guardian Gloves: 40 Heavy Leather, 10 Cured Heavy Hide, 10 Silken Thread
#  175-185 10 Barbaric Harness: 20 Fine Thread, 140 Heavy Leather, 10 Iron Buckle
#  185-205 22 Nightscape Headband: 44 Silken Thread, 110 Thick Leather
# Artisan (205-300), from level 35:
#  205-235 36 Nightscape Pants: 144 Silken Thread, 504 Thick Leather
#  235-265 36 Wicked Leather Gauntlets: 36 Black Dye, 288 Rugged Leather, 36 Rune Thread
#  265-300 49 Runic Leather Headband: 686 Rugged Leather, 490 Runecloth, 49 Rune Thread

section Leatherworking 1-30

